---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import Term from '../../components/journey/Term.astro';
import LessonRef from '../../components/journey/LessonRef.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
const cleanPrompt = 'Run the tests and tell me they pass before you change anything. Then find what is unused or duplicated in this project: dead code, copies, files nothing imports, tests for things that are gone. List it, with how you know each item is unused, and wait for me. Then remove one kind at a time and run the tests after each. Change nothing else.';
---
<Journey chapter="grow" first="adds" title="The project grows" description="Every feature adds code and some leave clutter behind. Clean-ups and refactors are jobs you schedule too.">
  <Step id="adds" title="Every feature adds to the project">
    <p>One agent builds the club list feature by feature, each through the check from <LessonRef id="check" /> and on to main. The project grows, so each feature reads more of it before its first edit: watch the share of its <Term id="window" /> in the readout.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="junk" title="And some leave clutter behind">
    <p>From feature 7 on, each leaves something nothing uses: an old copy, a helper nobody calls (the hatched layers). Every later feature still reads it, because nothing says it is dead until it has been read.</p>
    <ForLevel is={['technical', 'engineer']}><p>Ask for proof that each piece is unused: no import points at it and the tests pass without it.</p></ForLevel>
  </Step>
  <Step id="clean" title="A clean-up is a job of its own">
    <p>It removes what nothing uses and changes nothing else, with the tests passing before and after. It builds no feature, so it has its own count.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-do="clean">Run a clean-up</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="refactor" title="A refactor changes the shape, not what it does">
    <p>The list page is the tallest tile: every change goes through it. Splitting it makes the next feature read less, and only the tests can tell you nothing else changed.</p>
    <ForLevel is={['technical', 'engineer']}><p>Run <code>tsc --noEmit</code> and <code>npm test</code> before the first move and after every move.</p></ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="engineer"><p>Keep refactors and features in separate pull requests, so a failing test points at one kind of change.</p></ForLevel>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="tests" data-val="on" data-default aria-pressed="true">With tests</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="tests" data-val="off" aria-pressed="false">Without tests</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="A refactor with tests first">Before you change anything, run the tests and tell me what they cover in the part you will touch. If something there has no test, write one and show me it passes. Then split the part into smaller files without changing behaviour, running the tests after each move. If a test fails, stop and tell me.</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="rhythm" title="Make the clean-up part of the rhythm">
    <p>Twenty features from an empty project. Move the slider and the line under the picture says at once what feature 20 will read.</p>
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="control"><span>A clean-up <output>every 5 features</output></span>
        <input type="range" min="2" max="11" step="1" value="5" data-bind="every" aria-valuetext="every 5 features" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Do this:</strong> every five features, a clean-up first. Send this before the sixth:</p>
    <CopyPrompt compact title="A clean-up pass">{cleanPrompt}</CopyPrompt>
    <Next from="grow" more={[{ href: 'wiki/test/', text: 'Tests', side: true }, { href: 'wiki/review/', text: 'Review', side: true }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The project, its features and how much each one reads are made up to show the mechanism.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
